# D-93. A nested method that captures host names and is not the host's model: its native function
# is the stub, and no return builds its node, so the host's call of it is refused, located (the
# model's own call builds its node: unit_make_adder_model_call).
fn: makeAdder (int: n) fn: (int: x) int
    fn: helper (int: y) int
        return: n + y
    int: q (helper: 1)
    fn: addN (int: x) int
        return: q + x
    return: addN

add: makeAdder 5
int: a (add: 1)
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: a; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
